      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This feature presents information for patients in a question and answer format. It is written to simulate actual questions that many pain patients ask and to provide answers in a context and language that most pain patients will comprehend. Issues addressed in this issue are why back pain surgery may relieve leg numbness but not the associated back pain, patient controlled analgesia, and phantom limb pain."},
